message: "If you use this software, please cite the archived Zenodo release and the associated manuscript."
title: "GCC simulation and analysis code"
version: "v2.0.1-noc-preflight"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.19744969"
date-released: "2026-05-16"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Tugan"
    given-names: "Mehmet Oktay"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0005-8665-3583"
repository-code: "https://github.com/oktaytugan82/gcc_simulation"
license: MIT
abstract: "Simulation and public EEG/PSG analysis code for the Gamma-Code Consensus (GCC) model. The NoC preflight-clean release includes the Paperpal/OUP technical-compliance manuscript update, synthetic balanced-coherence regime simulations, Chennu and DS005620 propofol analyses, Sleep-EDF state-geometry analyses, Mendeley disorders-of-consciousness pilot analyses, ketamine boundary-state analyses, DS004504 degradation-proxy analyses, spectral residualization, gamma-artifact controls, phase-surrogate controls, wPLI controls, phase-only analyses, source/CSD proxy analyses, reliability checks, derived outputs, and manuscript source files."
keywords:
  - consciousness
  - global access
  - neural dynamics
  - EEG
  - PSG
  - propofol
  - sleep
  - disorders of consciousness
  - ketamine
  - phase synchrony
  - effective dimensionality
  - metastability
  - Kuramoto model
